  "id": "vision-rehabilitation",
  "term": "vision rehabilitation",
  "definition": "Vision rehabilitation is support that uses low-vision aids to improve visual functioning, especially reading ability and reading speed as vision worsens over time. Besides visual function, it may also help psychological well-being by reducing the impact of vision loss on independence, quality of life, and depression.",
